{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-mass-energy-electron-check","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:mass-energy-electron-check","kind":"remark","title":"Electron: crossing energy does not determine energy","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-mass-energy","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-crossing-energy","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-mass-identity","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-mass-energy-not-crossing-energy"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-mass-energy","tags":["mass-energy","electron","trefoil","crossing-energy","information-theory"],"text":"mass-energy-electron-check.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:mass-energy-electron-check\"></a><p>The electron shows that crossing energy does not determine energy (<a href=\"#prop:mass-energy\" data-at=\"information-theory/speed-of-light\">mass--energy equivalence</a>).</p>\n<p><strong>Electron.</strong>\nThe electron (left trefoil <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{2,3}</code>) has <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n_c = 3</code> positive crossings, so its crossing energy is <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{E}_{\\mathrm{cross}}(e^-) = 3q \\approx 3.330</code> Skein units (<a href=\"#def:crossing-energy\" data-at=\"knots-particles-confinement/nucleon-derivation\">crossing energy</a>).</p>\n<p>Its energy is <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{E}(e^-) = \\mathfrak{m}_{e^-} \\cdot c_q^2</code>, where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{m}_{e^-}</code> is the framing-corrected trace of the trefoil braid class (<a href=\"#def:mass-identity\" data-at=\"mass-endomorphism/mass-endomorphism-opener/mass-endomorphism-mass-identity\">mass identity</a>). The trace is not a crossing count, so <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{m}_{e^-}</code> is not <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">3q(q-1)^2</code> (<a href=\"#rem:mass-energy-not-crossing-energy\" data-at=\"information-theory/speed-of-light\">energy is not crossing energy</a>).</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/mass-energy-electron-check.md","heading":"Remark","number":"22.4.10","page":"b/rem-mass-energy-electron-check","qa":{"counts":{"pass":60,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":17,"unknown":0,"stale":60},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}}}
